  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A soap bubble of the radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is formed inside another soap bubble of radius,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The radius of an equivalent soap bubble that has&nbsp;the same excess pressure as inside the smaller bubble with respect to the atmospheric pressure is____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The formula of excess pressure inside the soap bubble is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;here&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;is the surface tension and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is the radius of the soap bubble,&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fe68b362-be00-4470-9013-1aa6a694634a-image.png\" style=\"width: 322px; height: 231px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>T</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>T</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>.</p>",
